[Music]  if an underground organism of  unfathomable size were unearthed in the  united states you might expect  widespread panic at the horrifying  discovery or expect the us government to  block off the cosmic terror from  civilians you might not expect the  entity to be turned into a theme park  marketed towards all ages but that's  what happened with the thankfully  fictional mystery flesh pit national  park the name given to a creature of  indeterminate size and origin that was  nonetheless turned into a tourist  attraction mystery flesh pit is an  ongoing multimedia narrative project by  creator trevor roberts who you can  follow and support in the links below  the story of the pit is told through  flyers advertisements and posters that  rebrand the horrifying life form as a  relaxing family getaway and it's this  upbeat language around something so  blatantly terrifying that makes the  mystery fleshpit project so amusing and  so unsettling just the sort of thing to  cover at this spooky time of year but  since venturing into the darkness of an  unknown organism is a little frightening  to do on one's own edge will be joining  me for this entry he makes great content  about prehistoric life unique modern  animals and bizarre cryptids so he's  just the person to help investigate this  mysterious organism now let's begin our  dissent  unearthed accidentally in the early  1970s the mystery flesh pit also known  as the permian basin super organism is  located in west texas  discovered by oil workers the first  tours of the pit were given by james  jackson a small-time oil man and showman  the mystery flesh pit was then further  studied and reinforced by anadyne inc a  deep mining corporation who opened the  park as a tourist attraction in 1976  with assurances it was perfectly safe we  know how corporations are  in selling the park to the public  anodyne downplayed the horrifying nature  of the pit itself creating a friendly  cartoon mascot caver coop who assured  families the pit was nothing to be  afraid of the attraction was later  absorbed into the national park system  in the early 1980s which led to the  permian basin super organism becoming  further normalized  surprising absolutely no one thousands  of tourists regularly exploring the  inside of an unknown organism would  eventually prove to be a bad idea as the  infamous 2007 disaster would prove but  that's a story we'll get to later  for now let's try to piece together the  material the author has given us to try  and understand the pit's biology like so  many aspects of the pit the more  visceral reality of the organism was  glossed over with clinical language by  the professionals who first studied it  since an organism of this size defied  conventional science numerous new  disciplines were founded to help  understand it geobiology is the term  used for how the organism interacts with  its environment looking at this early  map you can see the lifeform possesses  muscular skeletal nervous limbic and  vascular systems similar to traditional  life at least on the top layers this  cross-section of the pit however might  just be a small fragment of a larger  more complex organism how large  data collected from a series of  boreholes shown in this diagram suggests  that in some places the organism extends  over 30 kilometers below the earth's  surface for reference the marianas  trench is only 11 kilometers deep indeed  the author suggests that the pit may  well extend into the earth's mantle with  some of the imaginary scientists  implying that the organism may be native  to the interior of the planet having  merely surfaced to the upper tectonic  plates for unknown reasons and despite  public assurances to the contrary  there's evidence that people working  behind the scenes long understood the  super organism to be dangerous at one  point in this fictional alternate  history the u.s government launched an  investigation into the feasibility of  using nuclear weapons to kill the life  form although only the cover of this  report was ever photographed the  conclusion seemed to be a resounding no  what made the permian basin  superorganism so potentially  catastrophic the answers may lie deeper  within  in the early days of the pit a mission  called project freefall was planned to  chart the organism to a greater depth  than ever before  a joint effort between the u.s  government and russian scientists the  expedition involved a six-person team  lowered into the pit via specialized  vehicle over a period of two weeks the  pod descended down the dark wet squishy  pit reaching regions that had never been  explored before at last the probe  drilled through a dense layer of lower  cartilage and entered an unknown region  of blue tissue a single person pod was  lowered into this opening the russian  pilot described a reflective and  prismatic environment of which we only  have a single image from this on-board  computer when the pod was raised back to  the surface it was heavily damaged and  the pilot was missing  the researchers concluded an attack from  an unknown organism was the likely cause  project free fall makes it clear that  the organic section of the mystery  fleshpit is merely a portion of the life  form and other regions are unlike  anything in the natural world it also  made it clear people aren't alone in the  pit  even above the deeper layers which  weren't available to the public hostile  wildlife was frequently encountered  large crustacean-like organisms were  spotted as early as the first  explorations which this early sketch  shows  in typical mystery flesh-bit fashion  however the corporate higher-ups turned  these terrifying life forms into part of  the marketing wildlife safety brochures  were handed out to visitors explaining  the exciting anatomical fauna that  dwelled in the pit and how to avoid  getting eaten at the foundation of the  pit's ecosystem playing a role similar  to bacteria in the bodies of regular  sized animals were macrobacteria unlike  regular bacteria you can only spot under  a microscope macrobacteria were  multicellular goliaths that could reach  lengths of 12 feet or 4 meters across  this educational chart produced by the  park services showcases the various  types of macrobacteria and the other  bizarre species that dwell in this  imaginary permian basin superorganism we  won't be able to cover them all but one  notable species is the mesogalil  tridecapod an insect-like organism that  gets its name from its 13 legs as this  faded wild about nature infographic will  tell you these pseudo-vertebrates are  almost the size of humans and aren't  technically vampires as this guide will  assure you although they do feed off the  pit and look like something out of my  nightmares in other areas of the pit  there were sightings of other more  dangerous species and even rumors of  human-like life-forms called marrow folk  which inodine inc strongly denied they  maintained the mystery flesh pit was  just like any other national park and  anyone who mysteriously vanished just  didn't read their brochure carefully  enough  with the permian basin super organism so  hostile to human life excavating it was  a challenge  a challenge that began with finding  people to staff it  as this oddly hilarious park ranger  recruitment bulletin suggests however  with the right benefits and incentives  anodyne inc was in fact able to find  people willing to enlist in the mystery  fleshpit park ranger program  what kinds of jobs did this entail well  why not become a park trail engineer  this anxiety-inducing position involved  using compact stent frames and other  highly specialized tools to create new  pathways within the pit to be a park  trail engineer required extensive  knowledge of caving geology and  macrobiology as attacks from local  wildlife were apparently common  for personal protection the laser scope  anatomical environmental multi-tool was  the most reliable defense  intended to blast new paths within the  mystery fleshpit this portable tool an  example of which is on display here was  frequently used to ward off aggressive  life forms to more safely traverse the  pit's interior anodyne inc developed the  internal anatomy vehicle or iav a  vehicle that could traverse the slickest  and steepest of routes  its maneuverability came in part from a  rotating mechanical joint that connected  the front of the vehicle to the  midsection  as tourism increased the larger  ventarial environment excursion vehicle  was developed which we know from  schematics used a set of twin  counter-oriented screws for propulsion  these safari vessels could seat up to  eight park guests and take them deep  into the pits with supposed safety  supposed being the key word here as a  mock-up of an incident report tells us  that vehicles were bent melted crushed  dented or dissolved at least on some  occasions maybe traversing the unknown  depths of a giant organism isn't a good  idea after all  well as kaver dave might say that's not  the right attitude for exploring the  funder ground for adventurous park  guests the opportunity of camping on  natural unreinforced trails was possible  with the interventarial tent shown here  in this diagram unlike traditional tents  this collapsible multi-sided device  could endure the crushing shifts and  deadly wildlife of the pit while campers  slept at least most of the time when  things went wrong emergency trail phones  were one way to reach the park staff  called lighthouses by seasoned hikers  these subterranean telecommunication  devices were highly advanced for the  1970s and indeed the study of the  permian basin superorganism led to  numerous technological breakthroughs  one of many lucrative results from the  development of the fictional pit were  tremendous advances in the field of  computer science in the early 1980s  anodyne began to release computers made  of nervous tissue taken from the permian  basin superorganism with four terabytes  of organic tissue storage memory these  machines were extremely popular  an even more well-known product exported  from the mystery flesh pit was amniotic  ballast a miraculous fluid from deep  within the pit branded as vita salve in  advertisements such as this one  the product could cure various illnesses  and was almost certainly safe to use  but the most notable service anodyne  offered was access to the mystery flesh  pit itself aside from hiking tourists  paid for access to the amniotic thermal  springs the springs had strong effects  on visitors who bathed in them including  making their skin healthier and giving  them a euphoric sensation as long as  they could take their mind off the fact  they were bathing in an unknown liquid  the true focus of the pit for most  visitors however was the lower visitor  center a gateway into the deep that took  eight years to construct with restrooms  a gift shop and even restaurants the  lower visitor center was the hub of the  national park  was it a good idea to suspend a several  ton building on steel cables in the  middle of the pit anodyne inc soon found  out  at last we've come to the 2007 disaster  and all that follows on july 4th 2007  due to anodyne's negligence  something as simple as heavy rain and a  faulty water pump caused a section of  the pit to flood to unsafe levels the  result was a catastrophe most had never  imagined the permian basin superorganism  began to wake up  imagine waking up from a long nap to  find hundreds of tiny bugs had built a  miniature hotel in your throat you'd be  pretty mad at 9 52 pm the lifeform began  a choking response due to the flooding  causing the entire lower visitor center  to be crushed and swallowed deeper into  its skullet but this was just the  beginning according to an incident  report the creature then started to  surface with people living all around  west texas witnessing limbs of the  superorganism rising from the ground the  scale of which is captured in this  impressionistic painting from a survivor  and then the creature returned to its  slumber likely lulled back to sleep by a  mysterious contingency measure redacted  from the incident report in the wake of  the disaster anodyne inc was dissolved  and the park was finally closed to the  public with people perhaps finally  realizing that hiking inside a giant  creature isn't such a good idea after  all  the author imagines that the region  around the pit has now become a ghost  town but behind fences some are still  monitoring it in the present of this  alternate timeline the permian basin  superorganism is now kept under constant  surveillance but who knows when it might  awaken once more  there's a lot more lurking in the pit  you can read about online and you can  follow and support trevor roberts by  using the links in the description below  or by purchasing something from the  mystery flesh pit gift shop and special  thanks to edge for helping me archive  this mysterious organism  i've been destined from the channel edge  i cover all sorts of topics and natural  history whether it's the extinct beasts  of times long since past the bizarre and  sticky world of the living or the  extraordinary dark places our minds go  to in the supernatural or  cryptozoological if you like curious  archive ben g thomas or tray the  explainer you'll enjoy me and my content  as well follow the links to my channel  in the description and comment section  below and as always thanks for watching  if you enjoyed this entry please lend  your support and like subscribe and hit  the notification icon to stay up to date  on all things curious see you in the  next video  you

